WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:06.550
Being a video archivist for the SCP Foundation
is one of the easiest jobs in the entire organization.

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:12.110
You’re responsible for viewing every tape
found in the field, every interview with an

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:15.920
anomaly, and every event log recorded by a
Mobile Task Force.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:21.280
If something passes your desk, that means
the Foundation’s going to want its contents

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:26.880
viewed, transcribed, and the original source
footage stored for preservation.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.119
Compared to the doctors working tirelessly
to push their research to the boundaries of

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:36.370
understood science and field agents risking
their lives elsewhere, your job of lounging

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:42.440
in an air-conditioned room, sitting at a computer
and watching videos all day seems pretty appealing.

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.469
At least, on paper it does.

00:00:44.469 --> 00:00:48.870
When you take into account just what it is
you’ll be transcribing, the grim realities

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:54.539
present in all Foundation careers start to
emerge in your deceptively cushy office gig.

00:00:54.539 --> 00:01:00.540
It’s no secret that the Foundation’s visual
logs describe unspeakable horrors within.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:07.549
Disgusting body alterations, gorey details,
and terrifying imagery are mainstays of Foundation

00:01:07.549 --> 00:01:08.659
files.

00:01:08.659 --> 00:01:12.380
Most are never conscious of the fact that
every log that’s been written out had to

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:15.039
have been viewed by someone in the first place.

00:01:15.039 --> 00:01:19.729
Those blank Redacted areas where your imagination
has to fill in the details?

00:01:19.729 --> 00:01:24.880
Somewhere, someone in the Foundation had to
transcribe that sensitive information in the

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:25.880
first place.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:28.259
That gruesome kill in the Task Force report?

00:01:28.259 --> 00:01:31.759
The visual archivist saw the footage before
they wrote it out.

00:01:31.759 --> 00:01:36.509
Sure, your job might be to watch the Foundation’s
home movies all day, but due to the sheer

00:01:36.509 --> 00:01:41.119
amount of visual materials the Foundation
needs to transcribe and catalogue, you’ll

00:01:41.119 --> 00:01:46.239
on average be seeing far more horrors than
the typical researcher or task force member.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:51.069
Instead of being assigned to one or two projects
at a time, you’ll witness an infinite slew

00:01:51.069 --> 00:01:53.729
of footage from across the Foundation’s
history.

00:01:53.729 --> 00:01:59.139
You’ll just be viewing all of the horror
from a distance, behind a screen, after the

00:01:59.139 --> 00:02:00.139
fact.

00:02:00.139 --> 00:02:02.099
But you don’t need to be told that.

00:02:02.099 --> 00:02:06.450
You’re a professional, hard-boiled, grizzled
veteran of the Foundation.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:11.980
You watch hours of footage a day, transcribe
it, archive it, and send it out to be inserted

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:15.319
in the various articles and files in the Foundation
database.

00:02:15.319 --> 00:02:20.810
You’ve lived through countless Task Force
missions, observed endless testing logs, and

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:26.459
seen everything from unimaginable entities
to the bloodiest events ever taken place.

00:02:26.459 --> 00:02:30.879
It used to keep you up at night, but at this
point, you’re desensitized to almost anything

00:02:30.879 --> 00:02:33.120
the world can throw at you.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:37.540
Maybe that’s why you were the Foundation’s
latest choice to transcribe the footage recovered

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:39.349
from the site of SCP-6670.

00:02:39.349 --> 00:02:42.209
You’d heard the stories.

00:02:42.209 --> 00:02:48.890
A series of tapes that other archivists were
flat-out refusing to transcribe, due to sheer

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:50.590
disgust and horror.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:56.480
They’d been passed down the line two or
three times, and now they came to you, in

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:03.500
a box of literal VHS tapes labeled with a
strip of tape that read “SCP-6670, RECOVERED

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:04.500
MEDIA”.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:08.829
You didn’t doubt that whatever was on these
was intense, since it was enough to get a

00:03:08.829 --> 00:03:14.920
few Foundation archivists to pass, something
that rarely happens, but you were sure they

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.280
weren’t anything you couldn’t handle.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:21.579
You inspect the box for a manifest paper to
see if you can gain any other information

00:03:21.579 --> 00:03:23.090
about the tapes.

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:27.400
Most of the time, the varying parts of the
Foundation’s research is kept heavily indiscernible

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:28.700
from one another.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:33.390
The right hand never knows what the left is
doing, so getting any further context to the

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:36.920
footage you’re about to review is oftentimes
necessary.

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:40.499
But the paper inserted on top of the box doesn’t
reveal much.

00:03:40.499 --> 00:03:49.280
It reads: “Footage recovered from the discovery
site of SCP-6670, Containment Site 86, Detroit,

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:50.280
Michigan”.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:54.790
That’s about as much as you’re going to
get, but at least it’s something.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:58.540
You take the tape that says “First” on
it, and pop it into the VCR.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:02.569
Yeah, you had to dust off that old dinosaur
just for this.

00:04:02.569 --> 00:04:06.620
The real anomaly is that it still works after
all these years.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:11.310
The first tape is overlaid with a title that
takes up the entirety of the screen.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:13.349
“HAPPY BIRTHDAY JEMMA!

00:04:13.349 --> 00:04:15.599
1988” it reads.

00:04:15.599 --> 00:04:19.060
The camera pans to a small infant laying down
on a cushion.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:23.199
You can tell from the brief glimpses of the
background that the house is dilapidated,

00:04:23.199 --> 00:04:25.320
poorly held together.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:31.370
Not the conditions a child should be raised
in, but an unfortunate reality that some face.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:36.280
The baby stares at the camera, wiggling and
making adorable baby noises.

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:40.889
You wonder if this is Jemma, the birthday
girl herself.

00:04:40.889 --> 00:04:45.960
Your thoughts are confirmed by the camera-holder,
who plays with and tickles Jemma, celebrating

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.210
her birthday.

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:52.520
The camera-holder asks the baby to “smile
for mommy”, which little Jemma gleefully

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:53.520
does.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:58.160
Of course, the one holding the camera is Jemma’s
mother, and the two are celebrating her first

00:04:58.160 --> 00:04:59.160
birthday.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:03.770
The rest of the tape is ordinary, with Jemma
and her mother playing and laughing together.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:07.390
Her mother sings happy birthday to her, and
the recording stops.

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:09.650
Well, that wasn’t so bad, you think to yourself.

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:14.759
In fact, taking into account most of the stuff
that passes your desk, that was pretty good!

00:05:14.759 --> 00:05:17.070
But that was only the first tape.

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:21.770
You’re intrinsically drawn to the next one,
wondering how this could possibly inspire

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:24.500
so much fear in the others who watched it.

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:25.539
Second tape.

00:05:25.539 --> 00:05:30.280
The shot opens up with a woman dressed in
slightly tattered, sewn together, formal attire.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:33.199
She’s filming herself standing before a
mirror.

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:36.870
The title reads “JOB INTERVIEW PRACTICE
TAPE”.

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:39.919
After the title disappears, she begins talking
to herself.

00:05:39.919 --> 00:05:45.080
She reveals her name, “Melanie Jamie G.
Parker”, and acts as if she’s applying

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:46.280
to a job.

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:50.310
Specifically to an internship at the Walter
Media Broadcasting Company.

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:53.680
You can tell from the sound of her voice that
this is Jemma’s mother.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:56.400
Melanie’s mock-interview proceeds slowly.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:06:02.430
She’s visibly apprehensive, chokes over
her words, and seems to be in great distress.

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:07.400
Melenie mentions that she turned 18 the other
day, and that she’s interested in applying

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:09.580
for a job as a news reporter.

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:13.690
Still, she can’t get the words out properly,
stuttering and hesitating.

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:17.110
She’s clearly distracted by something off-camera.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:20.870
Midway through her rehearsal, the sound of
high-pitched crying is heard.

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:22.370
It’s the baby.

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:26.840
Melenie assures Jemma that she’s coming,
and leans over to hit the button to stop the

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:30.220
recording before rushing off to calm down
the crying child.

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:33.070
Again, nothing horrible, you think.

00:06:33.070 --> 00:06:37.449
It’s difficult to watch someone so young
struggle with the challenges of motherhood,

00:06:37.449 --> 00:06:40.819
but it hasn’t made you lose your lunch or
anything.

00:06:40.819 --> 00:06:45.470
You take out the third tape, pop it in, and
see what happens next.

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:49.449
Another title: “A LETTER TO MY FAMILY [CUT
THIS]”

00:06:49.449 --> 00:06:51.740
Seems like it was intended to be thrown out.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:57.340
The picture comes in, showing a crying Melenie,
sitting on the edge of her bed in a white

00:06:57.340 --> 00:06:58.340
gown.

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:03.790
Sniffling up her tears, Melenie delivers a
message intended to be viewed by her family.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:09.069
You learn that her relationship with them
is unstable, and that Melenie has been on

00:07:09.069 --> 00:07:12.150
her own for months, potentially longer.

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:17.330
She musters out an apology to her parents,
saying that she’s sorry about everything,

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:19.849
for a party, for stealing their money.

00:07:19.849 --> 00:07:25.000
She continues to cry, but tells them that
she wants them to know that she’s sorry,

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.460
and that she loves them.

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:31.310
She addresses her sister’s caring attitude,
and her mother’s smile, but is hesitant

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:33.240
to compliment her father.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:38.550
She reveals that she hasn’t spoken to them
in two years, but she can’t go any longer.

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:44.199
She’s barely been able to afford basic necessities,
and despite applying for as many jobs as she

00:07:44.199 --> 00:07:46.069
could, she hasn’t landed one.

00:07:46.069 --> 00:07:50.160
Her personal savings are almost depleted,
and she can’t sleep at night.

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:51.420
Jemma’s getting bigger.

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:54.449
A lot bigger than any girl should be at two.

00:07:54.449 --> 00:07:58.379
She’s rapidly outgrowing her clothes, and
Melenie’s unable to provide her with the

00:07:58.379 --> 00:08:00.569
love and care that she needs.

00:08:00.569 --> 00:08:05.030
She’s halfway through saying that she wants
her parents to take custody of Jemma.

00:08:05.030 --> 00:08:06.610
But she stops.

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:08.360
She can’t get herself to admit it.

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:12.620
She stares at the camera, shakes her head,
and begins cursing.

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:18.120
Melenie’s voice gets louder, and she vehemently
defends her decision to keep Jemma for herself.

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:23.129
She’s not subjecting herself to her family,
who she clearly despises.

00:08:23.129 --> 00:08:28.030
Melenie continues to lash out against her
family, saying that she’s tired of them,

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:30.919
and that they will never find her and Jemma.

00:08:30.919 --> 00:08:34.270
She’s visibly shaking, her voice unstable.

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:38.700
Melenie’s made her decision - Jemma’s
staying with her.

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:39.850
She makes a statement:

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:44.640
“You should’ve seen how happy Jemma and
I were, how nice life is out here.

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:48.730
The sun’s so much brighter, there’s no…

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:50.460
no fighting.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:52.190
No screaming.

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:53.920
No… crying.

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:58.580
I took my daughter and I left all of you and
I am happy.”

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:02.130
In the background, Jemma’s crying is heard
again from another room.

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:06.580
Melenie, drained, looks in the distance, surprised
to hear that she’s awake.

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:11.100
She wipes the tears from her eyes and assures
Jemma that her mother will be right there.

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:14.620
She forgets to turn the camera off, and rushes
out of the room.

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:20.010
For the rest of the tape, lasting nearly two
hours in duration, Melenie calms Jemma.

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:22.880
Holding her and assuring her that she’s
safe.

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:27.070
Eventually, the camera’s battery gives out
and the recording stops.

00:09:27.070 --> 00:09:32.190
So far, it’s definitely upsetting to see,
but you haven’t encountered anything anomalous

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:33.190
yet.

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:37.230
Maybe the fourth tape will shed some light
on what’s going on here.

00:09:37.230 --> 00:09:40.700
You put it in, and prepare for the worst.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:43.600
This tape cuts in immediately, without a title.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:46.750
Jemma and Melenie are playing together in
Melenie’s bedroom.

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:49.260
What she said about Jemma’s growth is true.

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:55.280
She’s only two, but she stands at four feet
tall, with long and disheveled blonde hair.

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:59.640
Jemma runs across the bedroom, making noises
and pretending to be an airplane.

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:04.700
Melenie, for once, doesn’t seem to be stressed,
though she looks visibly tired.

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:07.520
The sound of a phone ringing is heard in the
background.

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:11.530
Melenie immediately snaps out of her happy
attitude and runs off to answer it.

00:10:11.530 --> 00:10:15.700
While she talks on the phone, Jemma is seen
peering into a small hole in the wall of the

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:16.700
bedroom.

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:18.400
She then moves offscreen.

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:22.230
While Melenie is talking on the phone, Jemma
tries to get her mother’s attention.

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:26.640
When Melenie hangs up, she notices that she
doesn’t see her daughter anywhere, and begins

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:28.520
frantically searching.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:32.410
Jemma answers, her voice coming from inside
the hole in the wall.

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:36.930
Melenie tries to goad her child from outside
the wall, but Jemma doesn’t listen.

00:10:36.930 --> 00:10:40.750
Eventually, she hears a loud snap, and then
a scream.

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:43.720
Melenie panics, moving her head into the hole.

00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:47.780
Jemma cries, screaming that she’s in pain
and that she hurt something.

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:52.040
Melenie tells her that she’ll get help,
and desperately tries not to panic.

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:58.030
She runs offscreen, and for fifteen minutes,
all that’s heard is Jemma’s crying.

00:10:58.030 --> 00:11:02.480
Melenie returns with a young man, who would
later be identified as her neighbor, John

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:03.480
Bates.

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:04.560
He carries a rope.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:07.140
Melenie directs Bates to the hole in the wall.

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:12.000
The two are clearly familiar with one another,
and Melenie assures Jemma that “Mr. John”

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:14.300
is going to help her out of the hole.

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:19.360
Bates kneels on the floor and inserts his
head into the wall, feeding the rope inside

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:20.380
the hole.

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:24.200
On the count of three, they tell Jemma to
grab the rope, and they’ll pull.

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:27.910
Seconds pass without a response, and suddenly,
Bates feels a tug.

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:29.420
She’s grabbing the rope.

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:33.730
Melenie and Bates pull together, hoping to
lift Jemma out of wherever she fell, but the

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:35.270
girl won’t move.

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:38.160
She continues to say that she’s stuck.

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:41.290
And neither Bates, nor Melenie can get her
to budge.

00:11:41.290 --> 00:11:45.050
Melenie, who is now crying, assures Jemma
that they’ll get her out, while Bates is

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:46.460
more reluctant.

00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:50.150
Bates tells her that they aren’t going to
be able to get her out by themselves, and

00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:52.450
the two begin to argue loudly.

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:56.580
They agree to call the fire department, after
all, they’re specialized in getting people

00:11:56.580 --> 00:11:58.540
out of confined spaces.

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:01.630
Bates tries calling, but the lines are full.

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:04.470
Meanwhile, Melenie continues to lose hope.

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:08.830
Bates insists that they have to call 911,
but Melenie knows she doesn’t have enough

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:13.200
to cover medical costs, and if they discover
the living conditions that Jemma’s been

00:12:13.200 --> 00:12:15.630
in, they’ll surely take her child away.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:17.710
The two continue to argue.

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:22.890
Bates suggests that Melenie phones her family,
which is the ultimate breaking point for her.

00:12:22.890 --> 00:12:25.230
From offscreen you can hear a struggle.

00:12:25.230 --> 00:12:29.420
The sound of a cupboard opening, and then
Bates hitting the floor.

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:31.670
Thirty minutes of silence follow.

00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:36.200
When Melenie returns, she's caked in dirt,
grease, and blood.

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:38.360
What happened was evident.

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:42.980
Melenie sticks her head inside the hole in
the wall, and assures Jemma that her mother

00:12:42.980 --> 00:12:44.680
will take care of her.

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:46.800
The next tape pulls you in.

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:52.000
The title displays: “HAPPY BIRTHDAY JEMMA
1991”.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:55.880
You recognize that the video is being taken
from inside the wall.

00:12:55.880 --> 00:13:00.760
There’s a small lava lamp, and a cupcake
with a candle in front of Jemma, who lays

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:02.150
prone on the ground.

00:13:02.150 --> 00:13:07.440
She’s more pale than before, and looks to
be about 5 feet tall now, and her shoulders

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:10.060
encompass the length of the space.

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:15.270
From behind the camera, Melenie sings to her,
and Jemma blows out the candle.

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:17.310
The recording stops.

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:18.310
Another tape.

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:20.580
“HAPPY BIRTHDAY JEMMA 1993”.

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:23.600
Jemma’s looking visibly ill.

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:29.170
Her eyes droop, she smiles tiredly, and her
body seems to be larger than the space its

00:13:29.170 --> 00:13:30.540
confined to.

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:33.680
A cake sits in front of her with five candles.

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:35.660
Melenie sings to her again.

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:38.950
The 1997 birthday tape is even worse.

00:13:38.950 --> 00:13:45.880
Jemma is about 7 feet tall, and her face encompases
the entire hole, with no discernible head.

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:49.570
Melenie sings to Jemma, who just wants to
eat her cake.

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:54.300
The sound of Jemma’s bones clicking and
cracking as her body contorts to the tight

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:56.070
space is heard.

00:13:56.070 --> 00:14:01.740
The next tape is unlabeled, but the Foundation
determined it to be recorded around 2001.

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:05.140
Melenie sits outside the door to her bedroom,
sobbing.

00:14:05.140 --> 00:14:07.360
Her bedroom is entirely inaccessible.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:11.040
Behind the door, the cracking of bones is
heard throughout the house.

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:14.360
She’s singing happy birthday to Jemma, who
is unseen.

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:17.850
Jemma’s voice can be heard, begging for
food.

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:21.260
Another crack, this time from the ceiling.

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:24.820
Dust falls from above, the house is giving
out.

00:14:24.820 --> 00:14:28.520
Jemma screams that she’s in pain, and that
she doesn’t want to fall.

00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:32.810
The cracking gets louder, and before Melenie
can finish singing, she’s taken back by

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:34.870
the horror of the situation.

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:37.890
Jemma begs her mother to help her, and that
her back hurts.

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:40.360
The ceiling’s about to give out any second.

00:14:40.360 --> 00:14:42.350
And suddenly, it does.

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:47.910
The camera tips, showing a ceiling full of
cracks, which give out over the next few seconds.

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:51.910
Melenie screams that she’ll catch Jemma,
but she’s simply too big.

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:53.850
Her form is revealed.

00:14:53.850 --> 00:15:00.950
A block of barely human skin and tissue, shaped
into a square mass due to being confined to

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:02.880
the walls for years.

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:07.740
You can’t tell that the entity before you
is still human, and most of all, an injured,

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:09.190
scared child.

00:15:09.190 --> 00:15:13.680
Jemma’s anomalous growth, when confined
into such a small space over a long period

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:15.990
of time, resulted in this.

00:15:15.990 --> 00:15:19.310
Jemma falls to the floor, crushing Melenie
in the process.

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:25.250
For the remaining four hours of the tape,
Jemma sifts and struggles, all while crying

00:15:25.250 --> 00:15:26.730
out for her mother.

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:28.880
The tape stops.

00:15:28.880 --> 00:15:33.320
Disturbed by the content, you know you’re
going to feel sick transcribing these tapes.

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:38.860
You check the corresponding database file
for SCP-6670 in hopes you can access it.

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:42.700
Thankfully, its within your clearance, and
all is illuminated when you read what’s

00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:44.510
already there.

00:15:44.510 --> 00:15:51.640
SCP-6670 is Jemma, described as a large, amorphous
entity made of flesh, tissue, and contorted

00:15:51.640 --> 00:15:53.010
bones.

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:59.060
SCP-6670 is confined to a small house in Detroit,
Michigan, where its been contained on-site

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:02.600
with a concrete wall constructed around the
home.

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:08.320
SCP-6670 was discovered following the recording
of the tape, when passersby outside the house

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:11.560
described the structure as “breathing”.

00:16:11.560 --> 00:16:15.550
After which, containment measures were implemented
and research began.

00:16:15.550 --> 00:16:21.360
The only access point to SCP-6670 is through
the doorway outside the bedroom, as most of

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:27.500
the house’s structure is either destroyed
or taken up by SCP-6670’s mass.

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:33.690
X ray scans revealed that SCP-6670’s spine
is extremely contorted and is assumed to have

00:16:33.690 --> 00:16:38.870
grown along the dimensions of the home, with
puberty assumed to have accelerated the growing

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:40.340
process.

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:45.920
SCP-6670 is largely immobile, and is believed
to be “hibernating”.

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:49.880
Its intelligence seems to be roughly equivalent
to a small child.

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:55.260
Inside the home, the tapes were found, and
the file describes them as awaiting transcription,

00:16:55.260 --> 00:16:57.180
which is your job.

00:16:57.180 --> 00:17:02.180
Beneath the section intended for your work,
is an event log, transcribed by personnel

00:17:02.180 --> 00:17:05.799
working on site with SCP-6670.

00:17:05.799 --> 00:17:09.949
The entity, after remaining immobile for so
long, had eventually moved.

00:17:09.949 --> 00:17:12.020
The log read as follows:

00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:15.809
“The entity rolled in front of the camera,
where its mouth could be seen.

00:17:15.809 --> 00:17:20.500
It’s surrounded by several strings of rotting
flesh and caked with blood.

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:24.669
The teeth are rotten, consistent with typical
patterns of tooth decay.

00:17:24.669 --> 00:17:28.889
A clump of black hair clings to the side of
its lower lip.

00:17:28.889 --> 00:17:31.509
SCP-6670 is heard speaking.

00:17:31.509 --> 00:17:36.419
The camera registers the sound as similar
to ”Mama, I’m hungry.”

00:17:36.419 --> 00:17:39.350
Its voice is that of a young girl.”

00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:43.960
You’re taken back by the graphic bodily
alteration described, when the realization

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:48.279
hits you that you’re going to have to watch
these tapes multiple times over to ensure

00:17:48.279 --> 00:17:49.860
proper transcription.

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:53.100
But then one other thing stands out.

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:57.549
A clump of black hair on SCP-6670’s lip?

00:17:57.549 --> 00:17:59.350
But Jemma had blonde hair.

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:00.870
And then it hits you.

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:06.639
You know that you’ll be in for many sleepless
nights after this is all said and done.

00:18:06.639 --> 00:18:14.999
Now go check out “SCP-002 The Living Room
&amp; the Most Terrifying SCP Rooms” and “SCP-2432

00:18:14.999 --> 00:18:19.659
- Room Service” for more super weird human
body-contorted rooms and spaces!

